e":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6 - 08e6cd1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.beta.mono (08e6cd1) - EndeavourOS #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 24 Nov 2025 15:21:09 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (nvidia; 580.105.08) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 62.71 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I compile Godot with the following command:\n\n`scons p=linuxbsd linker=mold profiler=tracy profiler_path=\"/path/to/tracy\" profiler_sample_callstack=yes`\n\nThen compilation aborts with the following output:\n\n```\nscons: Reading SConscript files ...\nAuto-detected 16 CPU cores available for build parallelism. Using 15 cores by default. You can override it with the `-j` or `num_jobs` arguments.\nUsing linker program: mold\nBuilding for platform \"linuxbsd\", architecture \"x86_64\", target \"editor\".\nTracy does not support call stack sampling on this platform. Aborting.\n```\n\nCallstack sampling should be supported on Linux by Tracy ([see the chart in the original pull request](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104851)), so this seems like a mistake.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Compile the engine with the above cmd.\n2. Observe that it does not compile.\n3. Remove `profiler_sample_callstack=yes` from the cmd and observe that it compiles.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis is an engine compilation issue, so no MRP to attach here.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/us